Installing VMware vCenter on ESXi

This guide walks you through the step-by-step process of deploying VMware vCenter Server Appliance (VCSA) on an ESXi host.
🛠 Prerequisites

Before starting, ensure you have:
✅ A running ESXi host (version 7.x or 8.x recommended)
✅ vCenter Server Appliance (VCSA) .iso file (Download from VMware)
✅ A system (Windows/Linux/Mac) with network access to the ESXi host
✅ At least 12GB RAM, 2 vCPUs, and 150GB disk space for vCenter
📥 Step 1: Download and Extract vCenter ISO

1️⃣ Download the vCenter Server Appliance (VCSA) ISO from the VMware official website.
2️⃣ Mount or extract the ISO file on your computer.

    On Windows, use built-in File Explorer to mount the ISO.
    On Linux/Mac, use:

    mount -o loop vcsa.iso /mnt

🚀 Step 2: Deploy vCenter on ESXi
Option 1: Using GUI (Installer)

1️⃣ Navigate to the extracted ISO and run the installer:

    Windows: vcsa-ui-installer\win32\installer.exe
    Mac: vcsa-ui-installer/mac/Installer.app
    Linux: vcsa-ui-installer/lin64/installer

2️⃣ Click on Install (for a fresh vCenter deployment).
3️⃣ Accept the EULA and click Next.
4️⃣ Enter the ESXi hostname/IP, root username, and password.
5️⃣ Select a datastore to install vCenter (ensure it has enough space).
6️⃣ Set up network configuration (IP, DNS, Gateway, etc.).
7️⃣ Proceed with installation and wait for deployment to complete (~15-30 min).
Option 2: Using CLI (Automated Deployment)

Alternatively, you can deploy vCenter using the CLI JSON method:
1️⃣ Edit the JSON deployment file (vcsa-cli-installer/templates/install/embedded_vCSA_on_ESXi.json).
2️⃣ Update ESXi host details, network configuration, and vCenter settings.
3️⃣ Run the deployment command:

vcsa-deploy install --accept-eula --acknowledge-ceip vcsa-cli-installer/templates/install/embedded_vCSA_on_ESXi.json

⚙ Step 3: Initial Configuration of vCenter

Once the deployment is complete:
1️⃣ Open a browser and access vCenter UI:

https://<vcenter-ip>:5480

2️⃣ Log in with the root username and the password set during installation.
3️⃣ Follow the setup wizard to configure:

    Single Sign-On (SSO) domain (default: vsphere.local)
    Licensing (or use evaluation mode)
    Network and NTP settings
    4️⃣ Once completed, log in to the vCenter web client:

https://<vcenter-ip>/ui

✅ Final Steps & Verification

🔹 Connect an ESXi host to vCenter
🔹 Verify that vCenter services are running (https://<vcenter-ip>:5480)
🔹 Set up backups and monitoring
